+The concurrency mechanism belongs to record-store, not this HLD. The selected approach is **whole-visit revisions**: each submitted visit edit names its starting revision; concurrent edits produce competing complete revisions for coordinator resolution. Tablet-sync and review-export depend on this contract: tablet-sync tracks base revision IDs and displays pending competing revisions; review-export needs a revision comparison workflow and excludes unresolved visits from the Friday CSV export.
+
+### Key Design Decision: Concurrency Policy for Concurrent Visit Edits
+
+**Context**: Two field workers may independently edit the same visit after comparing notes offline. The server must not treat arrival order as evidence of authority.
+
+**Options considered**:
+- **Whole-visit revisions (selected)**: Each edit names its base revision ID. Concurrent edits produce competing complete revisions for coordinator resolution. Preserves each worker's submitted visit as a unit. Needs minimal merge logic. Trade-off: even edits to unrelated fields (e.g., observer name vs. species cover) create review work.
+- **Field-aware three-way merge**: Each edit supplies its base state and structured changes. Disjoint field changes combine automatically; overlapping changes require review. Reduces review volume and gets more visits export-ready. Trade-off: requires maintained merge rules for scalar fields, observer lists, and species entries. Rules cannot capture all scientific relationships (e.g., species identification linked to cover estimate). Tablet-sync would send structured changes and retain base snapshots. Review-export would need field-level provenance and a review view for overlaps.
+
+**Rationale for selection**: The team prefers a larger review queue over maintaining merge rules that may silently combine scientifically related edits without noticing. The tenet "Do not silently discard a submitted edit" extends to not silently combining edits across field boundaries that carry scientific meaning the rules do not understand. Whole-visit revisions make the coordinator's decision explicit and inspectable.
+
+**Downstream obligations**:
+- **Tablet-sync**: Retain base revision ID per local draft. Submit edits with that revision ID. Display pending competing revisions when the server returns a conflict. Support manual rebase against the latest accepted revision.
+- **Review-export**: Build a revision comparison screen (side-by-side or unified diff of whole visits). Exclude visits with unresolved competing revisions from the Friday CSV export. Retain coordinator identity and contributing submission IDs with each resolution.
 
