+**Concurrency policy: Whole-visit revisions.** Each accepted submission becomes a new revision of the visit, named by a monotonically increasing revision number. A submission must include the `baseRevision` it was derived from. If `baseRevision` matches the current head revision, the submission is accepted as the new head. If `baseRevision` is behind the head, the submission is accepted as a *competing revision* alongside the current head — both are retained in full. A visit with competing revisions is in *unresolved* state. Resolution by a coordinator produces a new head revision from one of the competing revisions (or a manual combination), and the visit returns to *resolved* state with a single head revision.
+
+The server never auto-merges fields. All competing revisions remain fully intact until a coordinator acts.
 
 ## Submission and Retrieval
 
 Authenticate the submitting worker and validate field types and plot references before accepting a submission. Preserve the original payload separately from any later resolved or combined representation. A retry with the same key and identical payload returns the original acceptance result; reuse with a different payload is rejected.
 
