 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission for an existing visit omits a baseRevision, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission's baseRevision matches the current head revision, the system SHALL accept it as the new head revision and increment the revision number.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a submission's baseRevision is behind the current head revision, the system SHALL accept it as a competing revision and mark the visit as unresolved.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a visit has competing revisions, a retrieval SHALL return all competing revisions with author, receipt time, and baseRevision; it SHALL NOT return a single current visit.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a coordinator resolves competing revisions by selecting one revision as the basis for a new head, the system SHALL create a new head revision with incremented revision number, mark the visit as resolved, and retain the original competing submissions.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a visit has no submissions, a retrieval SHALL return a 404 response.
